Creating and Managing Users in Active Directory
An Easy-to-Follow Guide for Beginners
Step 1: Setting Up Your Virtual Environment
To create a Domain Controller (DC) and a Client Machine, you need virtualization software such as VirtualBox, VMware Workstation, or Hyper-V.
Download and Install VirtualBox (Recommended for Beginners)
Go to the VirtualBox website.
Download and install VirtualBox for your operating system.
Download the Windows Server 2019 ISO and Windows 10 ISO (available through Microsoft Evaluation Center).
Create a Virtual Machine for Your Domain Controller (DC)
Open VirtualBox and click New to create a virtual machine.
Name it "Windows Server 2019 DC" and set the following configurations:
RAM: At least 4GB (recommended: 8GB).
Hard Drive: 50GB+ (Dynamically Allocated).
Network Adapter: Set to Internal Network (so it can communicate with the client machine).
Install Windows Server 2019 using the downloaded ISO.
Once installed, configure the server as a Domain Controller using Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS).
Create a Virtual Machine for Your Client Machine (Windows 10)
In VirtualBox, create a new VM and name it "Windows 10 Client".
Set the following configurations:
RAM: At least 2GB (recommended: 4GB).
Hard Drive: 30GB+ (Dynamically Allocated).
Network Adapter: Internal Network (same as the DC).
Install Windows 10 using the ISO.
Once installed, join it to the domain created in Windows Server 2019.

Step 2: Download and Prepare the User Creation Script
On your Domain Controller (DC), open Internet Explorer.
Download the PowerShell user creation script (provided by your instructor or IT department).
Save the script to your Desktop and extract it.
Inside the extracted folder, locate:
PowerShell script (for user creation).
names.txt (list of users to be created).

Step 3: Modify the User List
Open "names.txt" in Notepad.
Add your name at the top of the list (e.g., "Gustavo ColonRivera").
Save and close the file.

Step 4: Open PowerShell as Administrator
Click Start, search for PowerShell ISE, and right-click to select "Run as Administrator".
In PowerShell, enable script execution:
powershell
CopyEdit
Set-ExecutionPolicy Unrestricted


Press Enter and confirm by typing Y (Yes to All).

Step 5: Understanding the Script
The script will:
✅ Read names from "names.txt" and create user accounts.
✅ Set a default password for all accounts.
✅ Place the users inside an Organizational Unit (OU) called "Users".
✅ Ensure all accounts are enabled after creation.

Step 6: Run the Script to Create Users
In PowerShell, navigate to the script’s directory:
powershell
CopyEdit
cd C:\Users\a-gcolonrivera\Desktop\UserCreationScript


Run the script:
powershell
CopyEdit
.\CreateUsers.ps1


If prompted, select Run Once to execute the script.
The script will display messages like:
sql
CopyEdit
Creating user: a-gcolonrivera
Creating user: jsmith
Creating user: mrodriguez



Step 7: Verify Users in Active Directory
Open Active Directory Users and Computers (ADUC):
Click Start → Administrative Tools → Active Directory Users and Computers.
Navigate to the "Users" Organizational Unit (OU).
Search for your account (gcolonrivera) using the Find option.

Step 8: Test Login with a Domain Account
On your Windows 10 client machine:
Click Other User at the login screen.
Sign in using your Active Directory username:
Username: a-gcolonrivera
Password: Password1 (default password).
If login is successful, your account is now part of the Active Directory domain!

Conclusion
You have successfully:
✔ Set up a Windows Server 2019 Domain Controller in VirtualBox.
✔ Created a Windows 10 client machine and joined it to the domain.
✔ Used PowerShell to create and manage Active Directory users.
✔ Logged in as a domain user to verify the setup.

